          "content": {
            "content_type": "text",
            "parts": [
              "Created both folders within `symmetries`, with three main documents:\n\n- [Research overview and goals](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-3/11_arithmetic_collision_rigidity/symmetries/research-overview/01_RESEARCH_OVERVIEW_GOALS_AND_TASKS_20261018.md) — 24 tasks covering all seven programs, with priorities, dependencies, deliverables and success criteria.\n- [Research progress tracker](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-3/11_arithmetic_collision_rigidity/symmetries/research-progress/01_RESEARCH_TASK_TRACKER_20261018.md) — matching task IDs, completed baseline results, current status and evidence requirements.\n- [S07: missing estimates and alternatives](/Users/ebbaker/Documents/shifted-zeta-positivity/papers/investigations-3/11_arithmetic_collision_rigidity/symmetries/research-overview/02_S07_MISSING_ESTIMATES_AND_ALTERNATIVE_APPROACHES_20261018.md) — detailed geometric assessment and proposed approaches.\n\n**S07 is missing a quantitative connection between its geometric identities and the physical pair \\((H,H_x)\\).** Its current identity supplies no positive curvature contribution, and generic first-order bulk energy cannot control the physical path observation. Additional theta constraints might repair that failure, but they need an explicit estimate applicable to the actual approximation error. Even then, an upper bound needs a certified nonzero approximation or independent signed input to exclude a collision.\n\nThe alternatives deserve different priorities:\n\n1. **Physical boundary winding:** the strongest practical geometric option, with an existing theorem and tested pilot. Its cost advantage still needs a fair comparison.\n2. **Constrained theta-jet evaluation:** the best new analytic direction within S07, provided it controls residuals and preserves useful cancellation.\n3. **Mixed Green/adjoint estimates:** plausible, but conditional on resolving the observation and boundary issues.\n\nAcross all seven programs, I still prioritize **S03’s arithmetic residual mechanism**, alongside consolidating **S01/S02’s demonstrated error reductions**. The tracker clearly separates those proposed continuations from completed results."
            ]
